<mxCell id="c74" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;fontSize=10;" value="Notes: DS1722 SERMODE is tied to VDDD for SPI mode. CE is active high and driven by GPIO PB0, not the SPI NSS pin. The on-board LED (LD3, PB3) and the MCU, power, and FPGA DIP switches (left open) are on the development board: see the E155 Development Board Schematic. The socket also routes CS (pin 3) to PA11 and RST (pin 2) to the RST select header, and the firmware drives neither." vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="610" width="300" height="100" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
